    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "Reconstructing pre-industrial climate is challenging because instrumental records are too short and traditional climate proxies, such as tree rings, have limitations in resolving low-frequency, long-term temperature trends, which are muted by standard data processing methods.",
    "method": "The authors reconstruct century-long temperature trends over the past 500 years by applying a Bayesian inversion technique, based on heat conduction theory, to present-day temperature data from 616 boreholes worldwide.",
    "task": "The task is to reconstruct temperature trends over the past 500 years at global, hemispheric, and continental scales using present-day subsurface temperature measurements from 616 boreholes.",
